# =============================================================================
# ~/.envs  -  Shared environment variables for bash / zsh / fish / nushell /
#             PowerShell, read by the single-file `config.{ext}` loaders.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.envs and edit it to your taste:
#
#     cp envs.example ~/.envs
#
# The file is read at startup by whichever single-file config you source.
# Missing file is silently ignored.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   KEY=VALUE              # export KEY with the given value
#   KEY="value with space" # double quotes are stripped; content used verbatim
#   KEY='value with space' # single quotes are stripped; content used verbatim
#   # comment              # full-line comments start with `#`
#   <blank line>           ignored
#
# Rules:
#   * One assignment per line. No trailing `;`, no line continuations.
#   * KEY must match [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*  (POSIX env-var name).
#   * Surrounding whitespace around KEY/VALUE is trimmed.
#   * Quotes (if present) must wrap the WHOLE value.
#   * Inline `#` after a value is NOT a comment — it becomes part of the
#     value. Put comments on their own line.
#   * No shell expansion: `$HOME`, `$(cmd)`, backticks, `~` are all literal.
#     Use the placeholders below instead.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PLACEHOLDERS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   {HOME}   -> the current user's home directory
#   {PATH}   -> the existing PATH (useful when prepending/appending)
#
# Examples:
#   CARGO_HOME={HOME}/.cargo
#   PATH={HOME}/.local/bin:{PATH}
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PATH HANDLING
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The variable named `PATH` is treated specially: split on `:`, each entry
# is prepended to the shell's existing PATH if not already present
# (deduplicated, leftmost wins). Always use `:` as the separator here,
# regardless of OS — the loaders translate to the platform separator.
#
# Variables that need other env vars expanded (e.g. PATH={JAVA_HOME}/bin)
# don't belong here — only {HOME}/{PATH} are recognised. Put such cases in
# your shell's rc file instead, where you can use native expansion.
#
# =============================================================================

# ---- Example entries; uncomment and edit as needed --------------------------

# HF_ENDPOINT=https://hf-mirror.com
# EDITOR=vim
# PAGER=less
# LESS=-R --use-color
# PATH={HOME}/.local/bin:{HOME}/.cargo/bin:{PATH}
